Insert the OPE into \(\langle\phi(x)\phi(0)\mathcal O(y)\rangle\). Conformal invariance gives
\[
\langle\phi(x)\phi(0)\mathcal O(y)\rangle
=
\frac{f_{\phi\phi\mathcal O}|x|^{\Delta-2\Delta_\phi}}
{|y|^\Delta|y-x|^\Delta}.
\]
For small \(x\), the \(y\)-dependent factor expands as
\[
\frac{1}{|y|^{2\Delta}}
\left[
1+\Delta\frac{x\cdot y}{y^2}
-\frac{\Delta}{2}\frac{x^2}{y^2}
+\frac{\Delta(\Delta+2)}{2}\frac{(x\cdot y)^2}{y^4}
+\cdots
\right].
\]

Meanwhile, differentiating the two-point function at the OPE insertion point gives
\[
\begin{aligned}
\partial_\mu |z-y|^{-2\Delta}\big|_{z=0}
&=2\Delta\,y_\mu |y|^{-2\Delta-2},\\
\partial_\mu\partial_\nu |z-y|^{-2\Delta}\big|_{z=0}
&=-2\Delta\,\delta_{\mu\nu}|y|^{-2\Delta-2}
+4\Delta(\Delta+1)y_\mu y_\nu|y|^{-2\Delta-4},\\
\partial^2 |z-y|^{-2\Delta}\big|_{z=0}
&=2\Delta(2\Delta+2-d)|y|^{-2\Delta-2}.
\end{aligned}
\]
Matching the three tensor structures yields
\[
2\Delta\alpha=\Delta,\qquad
4\Delta(\Delta+1)\beta=\frac{\Delta(\Delta+2)}2,\qquad
-2\Delta\beta+2\Delta(2\Delta+2-d)\gamma=-\frac{\Delta}{2}.
\]
Thus, for a nondegenerate scalar conformal family,
\[
\boxed{
(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)
=
\left(
\frac12,\;
\frac{\Delta+2}{8(\Delta+1)},\;
-\frac{\Delta}{8(\Delta+1)(2\Delta+2-d)}
\right)
}.
\]

