Since we know the value of the central charge and the conformal weights of the primary states, we can compute the partition function explicitly. Let $k=(k_1,\ldots,k_r)$ denote a partition with $1\leq k_1\leq\cdots\leq k_r$, and define $|k|:=\sum_{i=1}^{r}k_i$. We use the analogous notation for $\bar{k}$. Then,
$$
\begin{aligned}
Z_{\mathrm{Boson}}(\tau,\bar{\tau})
&=
\operatorname{Tr}_{\mathcal{H}}
\left(
q^{L_0-\frac{c}{24}}
\overline q^{\,\overline L_0-\frac{c}{24}}
\right) \\[0.5em]
&=
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} d\alpha\,
\left(
\sum_{\{k\},\,k_1\leq k_2\leq\cdots}
q^{\frac{\alpha^2}{2}+|\vec k|-\frac{1}{24}}
\right)
\left(
\sum_{\{\overline k\},\,\overline k_1\leq\overline k_2\leq\cdots}
\overline q^{\,\frac{\alpha^2}{2}+|\overline{\vec k}|-\frac{1}{24}}
\right) \\[0.5em]
&=
\left(
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
d\alpha\,
e^{-2\pi\,\operatorname{Im}(\tau)\alpha^2}
\right)
q^{-\frac{1}{24}}
\overline q^{-\frac{1}{24}}
\prod_{n=1}^{\infty}(1-q^n)^{-1}
\prod_{m=1}^{\infty}(1-\overline q^{\,m})^{-1}\\
&=\frac{1}
{\sqrt{2\,\operatorname{Im}\tau}\,|\eta(\tau)|^2}.
\end{aligned}
$$
We use the product formula for the Dedekind $\eta$ function
$$
\eta(\tau)
=
q^{1/24}
\prod_{n=1}^{\infty}(1-q^n),
\qquad
q=e^{2\pi i\tau}, \qquad \overline{\eta(\tau)}
=
\overline q^{\,1/24}
\prod_{n=1}^{\infty}(1-\overline q^{\,n}),
\qquad
\overline q=e^{-2\pi i\overline{\tau}}.
$$
